# Publish changes to GitHub

GitHub Pages serves `main` at https://benwilks81.github.io/BF6-Best-Loadouts/. After you change files in this repo, commit and push to `origin` before finishing. Local edits are not live until that push succeeds.

- Commit the files for the change you just made. Do not commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, tokens).
- Write a short commit message that says why the change was made.
- Push with `git push origin HEAD`. If GitHub auth needs the CLI, use `git -c "credential.helper=!/usr/bin/gh auth git-credential" push origin HEAD`.
- Do not change git config, skip hooks, or force-push.
- If the push fails, say so and leave the commit in place.
- If scoring or weapon/attachment stats change, run `node scripts/explain_loadouts.js` and include `README.md` in the commit. The weekly refresh already does this when stats change.
